1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,930
A Microsoft 365 outage took down Outlook, Teams

2
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:05,870
and other services around the world

3
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:09,050
Downdetector logged more than 7.7 million reports

4
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:13,010
in the 60 hours after it began, Broadband Breakfast reports

5
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:15,210
More than 90 countries and territories logged

6
00:00:15,260 --> 00:00:17,330
at least 1,000 reports

7
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:20,370
Japan's Digital Agency could not receive email

8
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:23,690
In the UK, almost all NHS Trusts lost email

9
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:27,550
and some operations were cancelled, Tech Policy Press reports

10
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,850
Microsoft's preliminary review blames a software

11
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,510
defect, introduced in July, in its network

12
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:33,910
gateway servers

13
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:38,070
At worst, more than 80% of those servers stopped responding

14
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:40,570
Microsoft found no sign of a cyberattack

15
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:42,930
For the Gulf, watch how much businesses and

16
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,090
governments rely on a single cloud provider
